			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>In reply to <a href="https://uncommoncore.co/unpacking-bitcoins-social-contract/#comment-185">Skip</a>.</p>
<p>haha i don&#8217;t think i summed up much&#8230; but if you mean thanks to @hasu, then yes, totally agreed!  i sent this article to close relations because i thought it did so well.</p>
<p>i watched a documentary in which they tracked down a satoshi (or an s nakamoto? i forgot) living a few blocks from where some of the cryptographers discussing early btc ideas were meeting in the bay area&#8230; i&#8217;d be surprised if satoshi was the person&#8217;s name who came up with btc</p>
<p>that said, i think the wavelength of social constructionism is not getting enough in this space, and hasu hits it right on with this discussion&#8230; one thing missing may be the epistemic revolution in terms of sociology data that blockchains capture, but that&#8217;s a whole &#8216;nother article!</p>
